    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1721 after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sweden">Sweden</a>, the Russian Empire grew to cover some 22.8 million square kilometres.</li><li>It spread Russian rule from the Baltic to the Pacific and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#central-asia">Central Asia</a>, and freed some 23 million serfs in 1861.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#autocracy">Autocracy</a>, rural discontent and the strain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#first-world-war">First World War</a> brought revolution and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a>'s abdication in 1917.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-tsushima">Battle of Tsushima</a> in 1905, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#russia">Russia</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#baltic-fleet">Baltic Fleet</a> sailed some 18,000 nautical miles around the world, only to be annihilated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

